# TTIKnowledgeVaultPaymentEntitlement v1

A vault payment record is Discord-identity-bound but provider-secret-free: no Stripe client, raw webhook body, buyer personal data, or ambient credential travels past its admission seam, only opaque `ni:` contract and evidence digests and the exact effect fields named below. A checkout invitation opens no charge; a Checkout Session opens no entitlement; only an admitted, non-duplicate, non-stale provider event receipt settles one.

VaultPaymentReadinessGate(activationStatus=admitted, evidenceBindings=8-of-8 discrete named bindings each a valid ni: digest, providerOperationalAdmission=witnessed non-synthetic decision bound to activation's contracts with 7-of-7 customer-observed test receipts passed, requiredEnvironment=bound, publicOrigin=production-https-exact, providerUrl=production-https-exact, commercialTermsFile=effective and evidence-bound)
  -> TTIVaultCheckoutInvitation(status=pending, discord=verified guildId/interactionId/userId snowflake triple, productDigest, activationDigest, offeringId, planId, orderReference, providerRequestId, issuedAt, expiresAt=issuedAt+ttlMinutes, legalEffect=private-checkout-invitation-only-no-charge-payment-entitlement-or-revenue)
  -> BuyerCheckoutConfirmation(session=matching unconsumed unexpired invitation, checkoutIntentConfirmed=yes, productDigest=same invitation/config).

At BuyerCheckoutConfirmation the gate's `liveReady` value forks the chain into exactly one of two branches, decided fresh (not cached from invitation issuance):

  Branch not-live: BuyerCheckoutConfirmation -> TTIVaultCheckoutIntent(status=qualified-no-charge, discordUserId, sourceInteractionId, productId, productDigest, offeringId, planId, candidatePrice, paymentCreated=false, revenueRecognized=false) -> InvitationConsumed(outcome=qualified-no-charge, intentId). Terminal; no provider is contacted and no binding is created.

  Branch live: BuyerCheckoutConfirmation -> CommercialTermsAcceptance(commercialTermsAccepted=yes, termsId=same activation.evidenceBindings.commercialTerms and config.commercialTermsDigest) -> VaultCheckoutSolicitation(type=Offer, actor=TTI_ACTOR, target=PAYMENT_PROVIDER_ACTOR, object=ServiceSolicitation{contract=providerCheckoutContract, offeringId, quantity=1, successUrl, cancelUrl, customerReference=orderReference}) -> ProviderCheckoutSessionReceipt(type=Accept, actor=provider, target=TTI_ACTOR, object=StripeCheckoutSessionReceipt{customerSettlement=TTI_ACTOR, offeringId=same, contract=same pending.providerCheckoutContract, requestDigest=ni-bound, id}) -> TTIVaultCheckoutBinding(orderReference, discordUserId, productId, offeringId, planId, providerActor, providerCheckoutContract, providerWebhookContract, requestDigest, providerCheckoutReceiptId, recordedAt, simulation; deduplicated by requestDigest against prior bindings, an existing binding whose discordUserId/orderReference/providerCheckoutReceiptId/simulation differ settles as a refusal rather than being overwritten) -> InvitationConsumed(outcome=provider-checkout-started, checkoutBindingId) -> ProviderWebhookEventReceipt(type=Create, actor=provider, target=TTI_ACTOR, object=StripeWebhookEventReceipt{law=same binding.providerWebhookContract, signatureVerified=true, supported=true, duplicate=false, rawBodyRecorded=false, buyerPersonalDataRecorded=false, customerSettlement=TTI_ACTOR, offeringId=same, requestDigest=same binding.requestDigest, livemode agrees with binding.simulation, stripeEventId, id, created=safe-integer, not a stripeEventId already decided, not older than the latest decision already recorded for the same requestDigest}) -> TTIVaultEntitlementDecision(userId=binding.discordUserId, provider=PAYMENT_PROVIDER_ACTOR, planId, status=entitlementStatus(receipt), observedAt, providerReceiptId, providerEventId, providerEventCreated, requestDigest, productId, evidenceClass, simulation) -> SettledEntitlementLedgerWrite(category=tti.knowledge-vault.entitlement-decisions.v1, witnessed=true).

Every stage closes before its successor; VaultPaymentReadinessGate itself is re-evaluated at BuyerCheckoutConfirmation and again inside the live branch immediately before VaultCheckoutSolicitation is built, so a readiness change between invitation issuance and confirmation cannot smuggle a stale grant through. Malformed, unbound, envelope-mismatched, mode-mismatched, or already-economically-claiming input settles as a typed TTIVaultPaymentRefusal{reason, blockers?} at its seam; an expired, consumed, or evidence-changed invitation settles as an unavailable- or refused-page response instead of a fresh transition. `entitlementStatus` admits exactly three receipt shapes to a consequence — `checkout.session.completed`+`paid`→active, `invoice.paid`+`paid`→active, `customer.subscription.deleted`→cancelled — every other event type or status combination refuses as having no admitted entitlement consequence. A `TTIVaultEntitlementDecision` whose `simulation` is true can be built but can never post to the live entitlement ledger — the record path throws rather than write it. Reading the ledger when byte custody is not injected returns an empty set, not an error and not a grant: absent evidence closes access, it never opens it.
